The '''Combat Training Camp''' is a combat training facility which players may access upon completion of the [[Biohazard]] quest. The camp is located north of [[West Ardougne]] and just east of the [[Gnome Stronghold]]'s entrance. It was established by [[King Lathas]] of [[East Ardougne]] to train his forces, and various [[Guard (Combat Training Camp)|guards]] can be seen within the camp.

==Transportation==
* [[Achievement diary cape]] to [[Two-pints]], open the door and run north-west.
* [[Necklace of passage]] to [[The Outpost]] and run east.
* [[Spirit tree]] to the [[Tree Gnome Stronghold]] exit the stronghold to the south, and run east.
* [[Ardougne Teleport]] to [[East Ardougne]], run north, then run west, take the bridge south and run west past the Chaos Temple.
* [[Canoe Station]] just north of the camp.

==Features==
The training camp has several level-63 caged [[ogre]]s, which can be used for training [[Ranged]], [[Magic]], and [[Melee]] (only when using a [[halberd]]). The cage has a [[Loose Railing (Combat Training Camp)|loose railing]], which you can use to enter the cage to retrieve drops and spent ammunition. Attempting to attack the ogres while inside the cage results in a message saying {{mes|These ogres are for ranged combat only.}}

Inside the training grounds is [[Armoury|King Lathas's Armoury]] which sells melee and ranged items, including [[Arrowtips|arrowtips]] for [[Fletching]], albeit at a higher price than other fletching shops. There is also a group of [[Dummy#Combat Training Camp|dummies]] that can be attacked for 50 [[Attack]] experience per hit. This can only be done six times total, ever.

There are several [[beer]] spawns on the tables in the camp. Entering the Combat Training Camp is a requirement for the easy [[Ardougne Diary]].

